"Found 8 tool(s) — call the one you need directly (params below); it activates on use:\n\n### pdf_to_images [documents]\nRender PDF pages to PNG images so you can SEE them with vision. Use this when a PDF contains figures, diagrams, screenshots, charts, tables-as-images, signatures, or scanned content that `parse_document` (text only) cannot convey — e.g. you parsed a PDF's text but the user is asking about something visual in it. Pass `page_range` (e.g. \"3-5\") to render only the pages you need. Returns a list of page-image paths; then call `analyze_image(image='<path>', question='...')` ONE PAGE AT A TIME to view each (do not bundle pages — providers cap request size).\nschema: {\"properties\":{\"page_range\":{\"description\":\"Optional: page range like \\\"1-5\\\", \\\"3,7,10-12\\\". Merged with `pages`. Omit to render from page 1 up to the cap.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"pages\":{\"description\":\"Optional: specific page numbers to render (1-indexed). Prefer `page_range` for spans.\",\"items\":{\"minimum\":1,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"type\":\"array\"},\"path\":{\"description\":\"Path to the PDF file\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"path\"],\"type\":\"object\"}\n\n### tool_manage [system]\nManage dynamic tools at runtime. Add new HTTP or shell tools, list/remove/enable/disable existing ones, or reload from disk. Dynamic tools appear in the tool list immediately without restart. Use this to extend your own capabilities on the fly.\nschema: {\"properties\":{\"action\":{\"description\":\"Action to perform\",\"enum\":[\"list\",\"add\",\"remove\",\"enable\",\"disable\",\"reload\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"command\":{\"description\":\"Shell command with optional {{param}} placeholders (for shell executor)\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"description\":{\"description\":\"Tool description shown to the LLM (required for add)\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"executor\":{\"description\":\"Executor type (required for add)\",\"enum\":[\"http\",\"shell\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"headers\":{\"additionalProperties\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Static headers (for http executor)\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"method\":{\"description\""